---
type: diagnosis
title: Celly cannot compact a history larger than the upstream window
description: The native compact request is forwarded unmodified at 1.45M tokens and the gateway rejects it; a checkpoint past the whole context window is now chunked instead.
tags: [celly, compaction, cielairouter, context-window]
timestamp: 2026-10-22
status: verified-source
---

# Reported symptom

Celly (local AAP sandbox, G:\ciel-bridge-service, router 9385, build
0.2.51-nightly.20261022-060129.64ec9c4, provider cielairouter, model
_Walkie_Opus55-Sol61-Fast, context 872,000): compaction never completes; the
user asked that an oversized context be chunked.

# Evidence

- 08:41:47 runtime_compaction_control event=admission_paused phase=compacting.
- 08:43:17 native_compact_started, then immediately
  upstream_direct_request tokens=1458490 bytes=6307171, and
  08:43:20 anthropic_sse_upstream_error_event text_len=0.
- 08:50:10 the same request at tokens=1458498, answered
  08:50:12 upstream_direct_http_error code=400:
  "invalid_request_error: Conversation exceeds the known context limits of all
  eligible combo targets. Compact the conversation before retrying."
- No `compacted anthropic payload` line accompanies either request, while at
  02:20-02:29 ordinary turns did compact (1.45M -> ~683K, budget 716,750).

# Mechanism (code facts)

- prompt_compaction.compact_anthropic_body_for_budget deliberately leaves a
  native checkpoint untouched unless pcfg["_context_compact_context_rejected"]
  is set; the upstream rejection was the only authorisation.
- The Messages path (claude_router) only recovers an output-budget 400
  (context_recovery.recover_output_budget) and has no context-window
  recovery, so the 400 went straight back to Claude.
- The upstream wording ("Conversation exceeds the known context limits")
  also does not match context_compaction.no_output_context_rejection.

So an oversized compact request could never be compacted: the request that
would shrink the history was itself rejected for being too large.

# Change

compact_anthropic_body_for_budget now treats a native checkpoint estimated
above its model's whole context window (pcfg context_window / max_model_len)
as compactable, using the existing semantic chunked path. Checkpoints at or
below the window keep the old pass-through without any estimation, and
malformed/boolean window values keep it too.

# Verification

tests/test_native_compact_passthrough.py NativeCompactOverWindowTests:
over-window body is chunked (llm_compact_messages called once, tools dropped),
in-window body passes unchanged without estimation, malformed values pass.
318 exact-file tests OK (42 existing skips) including compaction, request
builder, transient retry and architecture contracts.

# Not established

The provider's own upper bound on a compact request is not documented here;
this change is justified by the observed 1.45M > 872K rejection, not by an
estimate of what the gateway would accept.

# Correction after CI

The first form applied the window rule to every full compact request. CI run
39792088196 (test (runtime)) failed
test_large_checkpoint_without_rejection_preserves_full_history: a translated
Codex checkpoint over its window was chunked without a confirmed rejection,
which that path's recovery contract forbids. The Publish run failed with it, so
no nightly was published from 57b39d4.

8045ba0 scopes the rule to Claude's own checkpoint (compact_kind "claude",
marked by provider_request_builder as _context_compact_native_over_window);
a translated Codex checkpoint keeps its confirmed-rejection rule, asserted by
test_translated_codex_checkpoint_keeps_its_rejection_rule.

# Follow-up: exact combo rejection

The deployed 64ec9c4 build still did not recognize the router's prose rejection
when a compact request reached the provider before the over-window estimate was
available. `no_output_context_rejection` now classifies the exact
`invalid_request_error` text, "Conversation exceeds the known context limits of
all eligible combo targets. Compact the conversation before retrying.", as a
no-output context rejection. Unrelated 400 responses remain non-retryable.

Verification after this follow-up: focused context-compaction and native
passthrough suites passed (42 tests); the runtime group passed 441 tests with
19 existing skips after removing inherited `CIEL_RUNTIME_CODEX_API_KEY`,
`CIEL_RUNTIME_ROUTER_PORT`, and `CIEL_RUNTIME_TEST_ISOLATED` test-process
variables. Ruff passed for the changed source and test files.

# Second stage: the live build still failed

Celly was confirmed running 0.2.51-nightly.20261022-142105.8045ba0 at 09:03
and 09:08 and forwarded the same 1,458,507-token request; the gateway answered
the same prose 400. So the preflight rule did not fire there: the checkpoint
kind was not proven at request time, and a native checkpoint still must not be
rewritten on a local estimate alone.

The error itself is the proof the preflight lacked. 81a270b:
- no_output_context_rejection recognizes "exceeds the known context limit"
  and "compact the conversation before retrying" for invalid_request_error.
- The native Messages path, on a no-output 400, compacts the rejected history
  through the semantic chunked path (_context_compact_context_rejected) and
  retries once under a fresh unshared transient-retry scope.
- The two pre-existing recovery branches are now an if/else; before, a
  successful window recovery fell through to the output-budget branch and
  raised TypeError('NoneType' object is not subscriptable).

tests/test_claude_transient_context_recovery.py
CielAiRouterContextWindowRecoveryTests: the prose 400 produces exactly one
second upstream request whose body is the compacted one, and an unrelated 400
is returned unchanged with no compaction. 330 exact-file tests OK.
